WEBVTT

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:20.330
Ta-dah! Ai-<i>chan</i>, look, look!

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.710
Check it out! This is the Kouka uniform!

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.130
I know. I have one, too.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.300
Guidance Week and the entrance ceremony
are finally behind us,

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.050
and tomorrow, we get to start classes!

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.680
She was so excited last night...

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.860
I'll at least <i>try </i>to
wake her up this time.

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:47.070
Wake up.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.200
Wake up.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.540
Well, she's not waking up. I tried.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.460
Good morning, Narata-<i>san</i>.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.880
Good morning, Sugimoto-<i>san</i>.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.050
Where is our troublesome Watanabe-<i>san</i>?

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.380
She wouldn't wake up.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.840
Excuse me, but I need to
get into your room!

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.510
Watanabe-<i>san</i>! Watanabe-<i>san</i>!

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:18.930
Come on, Watanabe-<i>san</i>!

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.980
Sarasa Watanabe...

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.690
Get the <i>hell </i>out of bed!

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.440
You can <i>not </i>be late
on your very first day!

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.780
Get yourself ready so we can
assemble in the auditorium!

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.990
O-Okay!

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:39.450
Wait, it's only 5:30. Do we have
exercises with the JSDF again?

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.370
No. We're meeting people who are
<i>much </i>scarier than the JSDF.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.170
Those Who Long to
Cross the Silver Bridge

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:19.390
Good morning! I am the first-year
student representative, Sawa Sugimoto.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:21.470
We're very sorry we're late!

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.890
Don't worry, you're not late.
There's still five minutes till 6.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:27.980
Our centennial class is so diligent!

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.980
Who are these lovely ladies?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.440
Those are the second-year students,
the 99th Kouka Class.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.530
Shh!

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:43.450
Sawa Sugimoto-<i>san</i>. I'm not surprised
to see you representing your class.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.580
Thank you.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:50.670
The faculty told me the highest
exam scorer earns that privilege.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:52.460
It's my honor to hold this position.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.840
Good morning, first-years.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.840
I'm the second-year representative,
Tomomi Takei.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.220
Today, in accordance
with school tradition,

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.560
we will be showing you how to
properly perform your duties

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:06.020
during morning cleaning.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.520
Thank you for your time!

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.440
Thank you!

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.730
Thank you!

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:20.070
I'll be a top star!

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.320
It's our pleasure.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:26.080
Each first-year has been assigned
a second-year student advisor.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:32.130
They will support you and give you advice
throughout your next year here.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:35.590
Excuse me! Who's my big sister?

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:37.760
There she goes, right on schedule.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:41.840
Your second-year advisor can
make your life heaven or a living hell.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.470
Sheesh, Risa, you're always so scary.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:47.520
Right, when your name is called,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.020
come forward to meet your advisor and
go to the location you'll be cleaning.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.100
Japanese Room

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.400
I'll be your advisor.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.320
I'm Hijiri Nojima, vice-president of
the second-year class.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:58.740
It's so good to meet you!

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.990
It's nice to meet you, too.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:05.450
Your eyelashes are so long, Narata-<i>san</i>,
and your skin is so pale!

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.750
No wonder you got to be in JPX!

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:08.870
Thanks.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:13.040
You know, everyone was fighting over
who got to be your big sister.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.040
We did a rock-paper-scissors
tournament for it, and I won!

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:19.800
I felt like I'd been chosen
to be the center for JPX!

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:21.300
Okay.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.850
Are you not a morning person? Do you have
low blood pressure or something?

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:26.930
Neither.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:30.520
I'm a <i>huge </i>JPX fan.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:34.440
If I hadn't gotten into Kouka,
I would've auditioned for them!

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:40.740
I mean, everyone in JPX is so cute and
lively, with their big, sparkling smiles!

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:45.240
That's why I'm so honored
to be your big sister for the next...

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.040
You weren't one of my fans, then.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:48.870
Huh?

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.880
You should start sweeping
from one side of the room.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:00.590
And don't whack it on the ground.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:03.050
Okay. I've never cleaned a room before.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.840
I can tell.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:09.010
So why are you so sure
I wasn't one of your fans?

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:14.020
Because I'm not lively and
I don't have a big, sparkling smile.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:19.190
I'm guessing you're a fan
of Momo Kozono-<i>chan</i>.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.780
W-Well, I liked you, too!

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:25.110
Your whole 'not smiling' thing
made you this cool-headed beauty!

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.700
Don't worry, I don't mind.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:33.080
So do you want to play women
as a <i>musume-yaku</i>, then?

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.210
I don't care.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.040
You don't care?

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.170
I don't care what kind of roles I play.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:41.000
Really?

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:45.800
Well, I think you'll be glad you got me
for this year, and not someone else.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:50.220
Some second-years are going to be
really mean to their first-years.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:54.560
The competition starts
long before you get into the Troupe.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.860
It started the moment
you got into this school.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:02.320
But I don't think you'll have to
worry about it, Narata-<i>san</i>.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:06.450
C'mon, silly! This is how you use a broom.

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:10.410
Leave some space between your hands,
and place your dominant hand here.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:16.710
I'm Risa Nakayama,
and I'll be your student advisor.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:20.710
Yay, my advisor's a Latin beauty
with a rockin' bod!

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.420
And I hate when people point that out.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:26.760
You're going to spend
the next two hours before class

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:29.140
cleaning the traditional dance classroom.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:31.220
First, sweep the floor.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:35.810
Then, use a hairpin to get the gunk out of
the cracks and wipe down the floorboards.

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:38.440
After that, you'll get the dust out of
the window cracks with these brushes,

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:40.980
then polish the mirror
until it's pristine!

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.030
I have two hours to do
that all by myself?!

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:43.860
Yep.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:45.150
I'll give it all I've got!

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.030
This is taking forever.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:55.830
It better not, or you'll be late to class.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.540
That'd be a <i>big </i>problem!

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:01.380
How tall are you?

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:04.090
I'm 178 centimeters tall!

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:05.210
And how old are you?

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.880
Fifteen!

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:12.640
I got in when I was in 12th grade,
so I'm 19. I'll be 20 next year.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:13.930
It sucks.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:17.770
Why? You're brimming with
mature ladylike energy!

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:19.440
Cut the chatter.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:24.360
Right! I just really like
talking with you, Risa-<i>senpai</i>!

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.570
Well, I don't.

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.860
Then I'll find something
you'll like talking about!

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.320
Don't bother.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:35.740
Figured! I'd better focus on this
cleaning, or it really <i>will </i>take forever!

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.040
You wanna be Oscar, huh?

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:42.790
Yes! I came to this school so I could
learn how to play Lady Os--

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.460
Well, you won't.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.260
Huh?

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:50.220
You'll never play Oscar.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.230
It will never happen! Not ever!

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:05.520
It doesn't matter how good you are,
or how much natural talent you possess!

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:09.280
No way in the world will you <i>ever</i>
be able to play Sukeroku!

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.240
Watanabe-<i>san</i>?

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:16.910
Watanabe-<i>san</i>, you okay?

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.290
Hey, Watanabe-<i>san</i>!

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:25.960
Why? Why can't I be Lady Oscar?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.130
Look, stop crying!

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:32.220
They're gonna think I'm bullying you!

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:36.600
She's too tall to play Lady Oscar.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:40.230
The actress playing André
would have to be taller than her,

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.850
Why can't I play her?

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:41.850
and that's not happening.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:47.150
Look, none of us wanted
to be your advisor.

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:50.610
Sticking out like a sore thumb
is a death sentence in this world.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:55.280
If I told her that, though,
how badly would she react?

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:01.250
Wow, so you want to be
a top <i>musume-yaku</i>, too, Risa!

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:06.670
Shh! Don't tell anyone yet, Hijiri!
I'm still kinda shy about it.

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:08.630
They're all gonna say
it doesn't fit my personality.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:10.380
I don't think that's true!

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:15.800
You're gorgeous, Risa, and you're one of
the best singers and dancers we have.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.600
Y-You think so?

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:22.100
But your voice and look aren't the cute
young woman of a <i>musume-yaku</i>...

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:26.150
Y'know, you'd be way better off
playing older women as an <i>onna-yaku</i>!

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:26.980
Huh?

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:32.360
'Cause you're so sexy! But you're not
like, pretty or tidy-looking, you know?

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.990
You'd be perfect playing Jeanne,
or Carlotta, or Kurotokage!

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:39.330
Any of those evil villainess roles
would be <i>perfect </i>for you.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:42.500
Man, though, if you were
just a little taller,

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:45.580
you might've been able to be
a top <i>otoko-yaku</i>!

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:48.630
That was the day I learned
that only girls like Hijiri

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:51.050
had a chance of becoming
a top <i>musume-yaku</i>.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:55.380
Girls with angelic faces, strong
determination, and a mean streak.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:59.890
Why can't I play Lady Oscar?

00:10:58.550 --> 00:10:59.890
Uh, oh,

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:05.810
I know! You stood under the cherry tree
before the welcome ceremony, right?

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.480
Right.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:12.530
No one who's stood beneath the cherry tree
before they started school here

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:16.200
has ever become one of Kouka's top stars.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.870
That tree is cursed.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.530
That's it?

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.120
Yep.

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:26.080
Then I'll just have to
prove that curse is fake!

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:30.750
I couldn't be here if I was a guy,

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.010
but I was lucky enough to be born a girl,

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:36.340
<i>and </i>I got picked to come here!

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:41.970
There's no such thing as absolutes
when it comes to <i>can </i>or <i>can't</i>!

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:47.640
I'm not gonna let that curse hold me back!

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:55.320
Huh. 'Cause nobody knows
what you're capable of?

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:57.400
Well, give it your best shot.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:58.740
I will!

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:00.320
I will, too.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:05.450
It's almost time for class. C'mon.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:08.620
I'll help out so we can get done quicker.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:11.750
Thanks, Big Sis!

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.830
First-Year Lockers

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:14.920
I'm here!

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:18.300
Watanabe-<i>san</i>! I was starting to worry!

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.300
Here I thought you'd messed up again.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:21.550
Why?

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:25.220
If one of us first-years messes up,
we all get punished for it.

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:28.480
The second-years will yell at <i>all </i>of us.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:32.730
Your advisor seemed kinda strict,
so hopefully that means you did okay?

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:37.740
Yep! Risa-<i>senpai </i>doesn't mince words,
but she's really nice!

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:39.610
She <i>definitely </i>messed up!

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:42.620
Our advisors were
scary, too, right, Chika?

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:46.620
She stared daggers at me when I
dropped the broom earlier, Chiaki!

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.290
The world of Kouka is
really competitive and intense...

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:54.170
But your advisor looked
really nice, Narata-<i>san</i>!

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.340
I'm not too sure about that.

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.680
How was our Lady Oscar?

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:03.600
Nothing special. She's still a child.

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:08.350
My, what's wrong, Risa? You look happy!

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.600
You must have it rough, Hijiri.

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:14.190
People think Naracchi could be
a top <i>musume-yaku </i>one day.

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:19.360
I'm not sure what you're implying,
but you're definitely mistaken.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:22.610
Naracchi has zero motivation for Kouka.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:29.710
Well, you never know what wind
will lift her sails in the future.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:40.790
First class is ballet.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:40.790
Wearing a leotard makes me feel so girly.
Everyone is so good at ballet, too.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:40.790
Kabuki practice all day today.

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:45.930
What do you want, Kouzaburou?

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:48.640
Those are Sarasa-<i>san</i>'s tweets,
right? Lemme see.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:53.600
I need to make sure you and Sarasa-<i>san</i>
are keeping it wholesome.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:55.440
That's none of your business!

00:13:55.440 --> 00:14:00.150
Remind me, Akiya,
who bought that tablet for you?

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:08.040
Ooh, a cool Latin beauty taught her
how to clean a classroom today.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:10.660
I haven't read that far yet.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:13.790
Wipe that look off your face, Akiya.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:20.590
Your biggest fans are older women.
No rude looks, or you'll lose them all.

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:25.210
{=1}A cool Latin beauty

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:25.210
{=0}taught me how to clean a classroom.

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:25.390
Sarasa-<i>san</i>'s 15, too?
She must be getting big.

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:29.140
She is. She's already taller than me.

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:31.020
Wow.

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:36.440
She was so tiny when she was
taking dance lessons with you here.

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:39.150
I wish we could've kept her around.

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:43.360
She's down in Kobe now... Maybe I'll go
sneak a peek at her one of these days.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.950
Don't be a creepy stalker.

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:47.370
By the way, Akiya.

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.200
Yeah?

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:51.500
Coming to you is getting annoying.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:55.370
Could you give me the password
for this account?

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:03.170
I'm Andou, and I'll be
teaching you about acting.

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:07.680
So I'd planned on talking about
Shakespearean dramas,

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:09.470
but let's do this instead:

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:12.520
Today, we'll introduce
ourselves to the class.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:17.230
Andou-<i>sensei</i>, forgive me for saying this,

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.480
but should we really be wasting
class time on self-introductions?

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:22.570
Ooh, I'll start us off!

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:28.870
Hold on, now. You all know
this is no normal school.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:31.540
When you graduate from a normal
high school, you've got options:

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:36.290
go on to college, find a job, take an
apprenticeship, get married, et cetera.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:39.460
But here, you've got two options:

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:43.420
Sink or swim. Stay with Kouka or don't.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:47.260
When you graduate,
you'll join the Kouka Troupe.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:50.970
That means you're stuck together forever.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:54.180
So I think it'd be a good idea for you
to learn more about one another

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:59.230
and start getting along a little better
early in your tenure, don't you think?

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:01.020
Very well, Sensei.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:04.150
Then, as our class representative,
I will start with my introduction.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.280
There goes Miss Bossypants.

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:08.450
I'm Sawa Sugimoto, and I'm 16.

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:14.410
My family runs a ballet studio in Tokyo,
where I studied ballet from a young age.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:16.410
Though they'd considered
sending me abroad to study ballet,

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:19.790
my life goal is to
perform musical theater,

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:23.420
so I applied to the Kouka school.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:25.420
I'm honored to be here.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:30.340
I'm Kaoru Hoshino, and I'm 18.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:33.470
My mom and grandmother were both
<i>musume-yaku </i>in the Spring Troupe.

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:36.430
But because I've got this great height,

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.940
I'm going to play male roles
as an <i>otoko-yaku</i>.

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:40.980
I'd also like to add that
I want to be an <i>otoko-yaku</i>!

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:42.730
All right, now.

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.820
I'm Chiaki Sawada!

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:46.280
And I'm Chika Sawada!

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:50.450
Chika got in last year, but I didn't.

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:55.240
So I waited a year so we could
both get in together!

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:58.040
Uh, I'm Ayako Yamada.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:01.000
I've loved Kouka ever since I was little.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:04.290
I can't believe I actually got in...

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.590
A-Anyway, I'm going to give Kouka my all!

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:09.340
I'm Sarasa Watanabe, and I'm 15!

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:12.340
I've always dreamed of
playing Lady Oscar...

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:15.180
Yes, we know,
you're going to be a top star, too.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:18.770
Right! I love anime, manga,
and period pieces,

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:23.230
and I live in Asakusa in Tokyo with my
Grandpa Ken, who makes tatami mats!

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:25.690
Oh, and we have a cat named Nono-<i>chan</i>!

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.610
She's super cute,
and her nose is always twitching--

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:29.990
You can tell us more about your cat later.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:31.610
All right, last one.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:35.330
I'm Ai Narata. I'm 16.

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:37.620
I've done ballet since I was little.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:42.750
I was taught by my uncle, Taichi Narata,
who's a ballet teacher here.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:44.540
That's all.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:47.710
Really? You know there's more.

00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:53.720
My mother is the famous
actress Kimiko Narata.

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:58.020
I was in JPX48 and was
13th in the election.

00:17:58.020 --> 00:17:59.680
After that, I quit...

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:04.400
They <i>made </i>me quit,
so I came here. That's all.

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:10.690
Wow, you were a JPX idol?! I had no idea!

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:12.240
Well, that's that.

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:15.990
Let's head out for our tour
of the Kouka Theatre's backstage.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.120
Huh?!

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:18.740
Backstage!

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:23.000
I got special permission to take you on
a tour from two to three today.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:26.420
You'll see that the stage doesn't
belong to just its actresses.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:29.300
What a wonderful surprise!

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:34.010
First, we have the costuming department.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:37.760
The embellishments are all
hand-sewn! Oh, wow!

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:41.100
N-No! I know those gigantic feathers!

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:45.350
Those are worn only by the top <i>otoko-yaku</i>
of the Winter Troupe, Sou Kazahana!

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:51.190
They're too incredible
to look at... I can't!

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:53.320
The bunny girl costume!

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:58.280
Wow! Look at this mountain of dresses!

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:03.040
It's just like Rose Bertin!
I feel like Rosalie!

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:04.670
Right, Ai-<i>chan</i>?

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.580
Rose 
what?

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:08.130
Okay, let's move on.
What do we say, everyone?

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:12.010
Thank you for having us!

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:13.630
I saw Naracchi!

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:17.930
She sure stands out.
I'll have to brag to my daughter.

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:20.560
Did you see that other stand-out girl?

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:23.890
The one with the twinkling eyes
and the towering height.

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:28.860
This is where the scenery department
builds the set: just backstage.

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:30.020
There's a set piece now.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:32.070
That's a long brush!

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:34.110
Yeah, I've never seen one
like that before.

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:37.870
Whoa, it's all Styrofoam!
But it looks so real!

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:39.700
You think so?

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:41.990
C'mon, Watanabe, don't get in their way.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.290
It's all good, Andou-<i>sensei</i>.

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:48.670
Gettin' praise from future actresses
gets us all motivated to work harder.

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:51.500
Great! I'm gonna be a top star one day,

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:54.380
so when I get there, I hope you'll
make an awesome set for me!

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.680
There she goes again.

00:19:56.680 --> 00:20:01.430
Well, all right! No goin' back
on a bold statement like that.

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:03.890
We'll be waitin' for ya then!

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:06.350
Yep! We got ourselves a deal!

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:08.400
Thank you for your time!

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:29.580
Hey, you idiot! Watanabe!
Don't go through there!

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:32.880
Watanabe! That's the stage door!

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:01.740
Watanabe! Get back here, right now!

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:04.910
And don't you dare walk out
on the silver bridge!

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:06.410
The silver bridge?

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:10.330
It's the part of the apron
that's separated from the stage.

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:14.920
Only Kouka's most dazzling stars
can cross that bridge.

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:22.300
Yeah, only the top <i>otoko-yaku </i>and
<i>musume-yaku </i>and a handful of others.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:26.520
That's where we all want to stand one day.

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:28.930
The silver bridge...

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.520
Someone's out on the stage.

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:40.200
Judging from height, it's probably
Yama-<i>san</i>. Pop a light on him.

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.750
To become one of Kouka's top stars,

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:54.750
you need hard work,
talent, star quality...

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:59.300
...and enough luck to be
given the right chance.

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:03.140
Sarasa Watanabe's stage presence...

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:05.050
...was dazzling.

00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:13.930
{=2}Ex-JPX idol Ai Narata
enrolls in Kouka School!

00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:18.030
I'm finally here in Kobe...

00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:54.620
Act 3: 
